course: dictionary
lesson: 4331
title: Spotting a grumbler
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A grumbler is a person who often grumbles. They complain in a low, unhappy voice about small things. Context gives you the clues: the sentence says «boasters and grumblers make things sound huge», so a grumbler makes small things seem big.
explain: Look at the words around grumblers in the sentence. Boasters show off, and grumblers complain. Both make things sound bigger than they really are. The quote «it took forever» is the kind of thing a grumbler says about a short wait.
explain: Other words mean nearly the same: moaner, complainer and grouch. Whinger is used in the UK and Australia. When you meet one of these words, ask: is this person always complaining? If yes, you have found a grumbler.
fact: A grumbler is a person who often grumbles.
fact: To grumble is to complain in a low, unhappy voice about small things.
fact: In stories, a grumbler is a moaning character who is never happy, often shown in a funny way.
fact: Grumblers can make things sound huge, like «it took forever» for a short wait.
fact: Related words: moaner, whinger (UK, Australia), complainer, grouch.
exercise: In the sentence «boasters and grumblers make things sound huge», what is a grumbler? | A person who forgets things easily | A person who shows off about what they have done | A person who likes to sing loudly | *A person who often complains in a low, unhappy voice
exercise: Which word from the sentence means people who show off? | sound | huge | *boasters | things
exercise: A girl says, «It took forever!» about a five-minute wait. What kind of speaker is she most like? | A map reader | A scientist measuring time | *A grumbler | A quiet listener
test: Which word means nearly the same as grumbler? | Sleeper | *Moaner | Painter | Dancer
test: Why does a grumbler make things sound huge? | Because they are always happy | Because they like being quiet | *Because they complain about small things as if they were big | Because they measure everything carefully
exam: Read «boasters and grumblers make things sound huge», then say what a grumbler does and find one clue from the words around it. | A grumbler sleeps all day, and the clue is the word things | *A grumbler complains a lot, and the clue is that they make things sound huge | A grumbler sings happily, and the clue is the word boasters | A grumbler is a teacher, and the clue is the word sound
